            <ArticleTitle>Mechanism of analgesic effect of clonidine in the treatment of dysmenorrhea.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>223-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Clonidine substantially reduces the pain and cramping of dysmenorrhea. The mechanisms for this effect may lie in increased release of analgesic opioids. It is suggested that perhaps a thromboxane synthetase inhibitor such as ginger which activates endorphin receptors may also be an effective treatment.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
